# Supabase CLI local-stack artifacts
# The WHOLE .temp directory, not one file inside it. `supabase start` writes
# a generated edge-runtime bundle to supabase/.temp/start-secrets/, and
# cli-latest was listed three separate times while the directory around it
# was not listed at all.
supabase/.temp/
supabase/.branches/
# NOTHING UNDER supabase/migrations/ MAY BE IGNORED — enforced by
# scripts/migrations-lint.mjs (US-2444).
#
# 00122_verified_storefront_listings.sql was listed here and never committed, so
# the sequence has a hole at exactly one number while the objects it creates are
# live in production. Every other guard stayed green: db-migrations.yml only
# proves the files PRESENT apply, the boot manifest starts at 00254, and the
# tracked-and-ignored check (US-2437) looks for the opposite state. A migration
# git refuses to see is a migration that exists on one machine.
#
# Removing the line does not restore the file — that needs the DDL read out of
# the running database. It restores the ability to notice. If a copy exists in
# someone's working tree it will now show as untracked, which is the point; the
# pre-commit gitleaks hook is what stands between it and a committed secret.

