# US-2284 [P0] — SIGNING KEYS AND BUILD ARTIFACTS ARE NEVER COMMITTED.
#
# extension.pem is the Chrome Web Store signing identity: anyone holding it can
# publish an update that every installed user auto-receives. It WAS committed
# (2026-07-13, e1dbc4da) and lived in the repo for weeks. gitleaks did not catch
# it on any run after that commit, because push-mode only scans NEW commits — a
# leak that is already in history is permanently invisible to it. That is why
# .github/workflows/secret-scan-history.yml now sweeps the FULL history on a
# schedule, and why these patterns are broad rather than path-specific.
#
# Removing a key from the index does NOT un-leak it. Rotation is the fix; the
# ignore rule only stops the next one.
*.pem
*.crx
*.p12
*.keystore
*.jks
ios-screenshots/**/*.zip

# scripts/archive-passing-stories.mjs writes these before it rewrites the two
# backlog files. They are a local undo for one command, not history — the
# history is prd.archive.json itself, which IS tracked. Committing a 4 MB copy
# of it on every archive run would be pure noise.
prd.json.bak
prd.archive.json.bak
